#: 38440b0fb4a34704bd4d984f4287968b
msgid "Linear algebra API"
msgstr "线性代数 API"

#: 46d4fa4248c2417a807879292d2b5431
msgid ""
"The `jittor.linalg` module covers matrix decompositions, linear solves, "
"eigenvalue routines, norms, and Einstein summation."
msgstr ""

#: 353d51bf753a42acbd291620244a6375
msgid ":py:obj:`inv <jittor.linalg.inv>`\\ \\(x\\)"
msgstr ""

#: 01895fe7639d4c80866e776ff1531545
msgid "calculate the inverse of x."
msgstr ""

#: e20d78c9b4de4ecd9793b9a6c58260fb
msgid ":py:obj:`pinv <jittor.linalg.pinv>`\\ \\(x\\)"
msgstr ""

#: 00be67d6b90c450d9767e15578b42874
msgid "calculate the pseudo-inverse of a x."
msgstr ""

#: 444ca6fc9c1045a98a0afe8c0d8d2567
msgid ":py:obj:`solve <jittor.linalg.solve>`\\ \\(a\\, b\\)"
msgstr ""

#: fb96500ad8bf407f93db6808a0324cfb
msgid ""
"Solve a linear matrix equation Ax = B.This is done by calculating x = "
"A^-1B.So A must not be singular."
msgstr ""

#: ccddceea7882441c9bb0cd0bad635c30
msgid ":py:obj:`det <jittor.linalg.det>`\\ \\(x\\)"
msgstr ""

#: 38bf7c3287f845da956f921e1477a898
msgid "calculate the determinant of x."
msgstr ""

#: 11ca87e9eb0142f6ad5937517b2290b1
msgid ":py:obj:`slogdet <jittor.linalg.slogdet>`\\ \\(x\\)"
msgstr ""

#: 046c353a2d5f482dbe3c68d439c7370e
msgid "calculate the sign and log of the determinant of x."
msgstr ""

#: 55338571c8f24afebabf59c23b60cdb5
msgid ":py:obj:`cholesky <jittor.linalg.cholesky>`\\ \\(x\\)"
msgstr ""

#: 2967e551665e45af85b6e8a517a90e2b
msgid ""
"do Cholesky decomposition of x in the form of below formula: x = LL^T x must"
" be a Hermite and positive-definite matrix."
msgstr ""

#: 65b02dae40a54c7fa47dcdf291e66227
msgid ":py:obj:`qr <jittor.linalg.qr>`\\ \\(x\\)"
msgstr ""

#: 3d0044eb3c914f2da440ba845036a100
msgid ""
"do the qr factorization of x in the below formula: x = QR where Q is "
"orthogonal matrix and R is upper-triangle matrix."
msgstr ""

#: 8757a753ef7b44abb9bb8e3c357e323d
msgid ""
":py:obj:`svd <jittor.linalg.svd>`\\ \\(x\\[\\, full\\_matrices\\, "
"compute\\_uv\\, driver\\]\\)"
msgstr ""

#: e36555c72a6349b99679600741d4323e
msgid "Singular Value Decomposition: ``A = U @ diag(S) @ Vh``."
msgstr ""

#: a7d90f07ecc743fea56205943440c1b2
msgid ":py:obj:`eigh <jittor.linalg.eigh>`\\ \\(x\\)"
msgstr ""

#: d591ec667f4942e281a83a54c7213eaf
msgid "calculate the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of x."
msgstr ""

#: 60809f148264480e86454b8a8b71a513
msgid ":py:obj:`norm <jittor.linalg.norm>`\\ \\(x\\[\\, ord\\, dim\\, keepdim\\]\\)"
msgstr ""

#: 2ce0a24e2836407c97cbcb37f8245aa1 2ea7494f607d4e2298b76df110cf258e
msgid "General ``torch.linalg.norm`` / ``numpy.linalg.norm`` dispatcher."
msgstr ""

#: f4057c3edbef4575bc391c111d485545
msgid ":py:obj:`einsum <jittor.linalg.einsum>`\\ \\(equation\\, \\*operands\\)"
msgstr ""

#: 42a8a92f3f2949ecb8a55c4e01ab3111 61d463aa4b554123bd3484d122119f0a
msgid "Evaluate the Einstein summation convention on the operands."
msgstr ""

#: c8982531ffa14d32a2a3fba3aa6d3c5b
msgid ""
"Singular Value Decomposition: ``A = U @ diag(S) @ Vh``. Returns the same "
"named ``(U, S, Vh)`` result as ``torch.linalg.svd`` (and it also unpacks as "
"a plain 3-tuple ``u, s, v``, preserving every existing jittor caller)."
msgstr ""

#: f81f70dea6f244f388fade27720c9624
msgid "For ``A`` of shape ``(...,M,N)`` with ``K = min(M, N)``:"
msgstr ""

#: 520f72c51d534e6cb4b84714f9c4767b
msgid ""
"``full_matrices=False`` (default, reduced / \"thin\"): ``U`` is "
"``(...,M,K)``, ``Vh`` is ``(...,K,N)``, ``S`` is ``(...,K)``."
msgstr ""

#: 0d56cd12c61047ad860e0234c3a270bd
msgid ""
"``full_matrices=True``: ``U`` is ``(...,M,M)``, ``Vh`` is ``(...,N,N)``, "
"``S`` is ``(...,K)``."
msgstr ""

#: 9a11165b2244437dbf862496cb085785
msgid ""
"``torch.linalg.svd`` defaults to ``full_matrices=True``; this jittor- native"
" entry point keeps the historical reduced default so that the differentiable"
" path and all jittor callers (``matrix_rank``/``cond``/ ``matrix_norm``/the "
"native ``test_linalg`` suite) are unchanged. Pass ``full_matrices=True`` "
"explicitly for torch's full shapes. (The torch- facing ``torch.linalg.svd`` "
"default is meant to be supplied at the torch-compat boundary.)"
msgstr ""

#: 1bb5ffb9a9a34e908674b9788d84dbbc
msgid ""
"``S`` is sorted in descending order. The reduced form (and the square case, "
"where reduced == full) is differentiable; the full form on a *non-square* "
"matrix is computed via numpy without a gradient on ``U``/``Vh`` (the extra "
"orthogonal-complement columns/rows have no unique gradient) — use "
"``full_matrices=False`` or :func:`svdvals` when gradients are needed."
msgstr ""

#: 411a833c62114e84aef1b4946153b03c bdb24f374cf64b56bae4dfd46671a97d
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: 7aac1cca276b47019fc4022fcf676aa4
msgid "``(...,M,N)`` real matrix (or ``nn.ComplexNumber``)."
msgstr ""

#: 3a02c6a777804ff3a61b9b2742e14a27
msgid "see above. Default ``False`` (reduced)."
msgstr ""

#: f59c1813a2b24db9af2e57e96f842c44
msgid ""
"if ``False``, only ``S`` is meaningful (``U`` and ``Vh`` are still returned "
"for shape compatibility but may be skipped)."
msgstr ""

#: 84267f31d2d54ba39a4937c97a4f06e6
msgid "accepted for torch signature compatibility (ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: 00405edc71c4494aafb731b496cde7a5 0f36a844d4c74df9bb28b9d5f8dd1eb3
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: 785ce76f02284e919603a2ebbbc674ac
msgid "named tuple ``SVD(U, S, Vh)``."
msgstr ""

#: 2dc7a7066df241b08407f7f08af3e981
msgid ""
"calculate the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of x. :param x (...,M,M): "
":return:w, v. w (...,M) : the eigenvalues. v (...,M,M) : normalized "
"eigenvectors."
msgstr ""

#: b25cd854b7b740f39887b25001034300
msgid "calculate the inverse of x. :param x (...,M,M): :return:x^-1 (...,M,M)."
msgstr ""

#: b671a7bdae39449f9c3b90402fddd081
msgid ""
"calculate the pseudo-inverse of a x. :param x (...,M,N) :return: x's pinv "
"(...N,M)"
msgstr ""

#: 4832a6fd48044625bf98db69f8657761
msgid "Behaviour (matching torch/numpy):"
msgstr ""

#: c30f962d7102440f85b4dbe024724612
msgid ""
"``dim`` is a 2-tuple, or ``dim is None`` and ``x`` is 2-D: matrix norm "
"(default ``ord`` is the Frobenius norm), see :func:`matrix_norm`."
msgstr ""

#: 6116ae9271f84176bc480e87cd57f3a5
msgid ""
"``dim`` is an int, or ``dim is None`` and ``x`` is 1-D, or ``ord`` is set "
"with ``dim is None``: vector norm (default ``ord`` is 2), see "
":func:`vector_norm`."
msgstr ""

#: 43fbbdab6ed64dcdafa70de6d8c78632
msgid ""
"``dim is None`` and ``ord is None``: the 2-norm of the flattened tensor "
"(Frobenius), built from native jittor ops."
msgstr ""

#: 8148b95412084338958d7bf787965845
msgid "input tensor."
msgstr ""

#: b34409e9611d4e5a8b44e39a1d0e4922
msgid ""
"order of the norm; meaning depends on whether a matrix or a vector norm is "
"selected (see :func:`matrix_norm` / :func:`vector_norm`)."
msgstr ""

#: 4faf9c0f54e44a0799a5ad9f801a1fe8
msgid "axis/axes defining the norm."
msgstr ""

#: 5c02f81fc4e243ac91c82a2087718a44
msgid "keep reduced dims as size-1."
msgstr ""

#: d1665e2b941848febaefa499bba4dc13
msgid "the requested norm."
msgstr ""

#: c3b6e5fb959446ab89f2a708554bade1
msgid "calculate the determinant of x. :param x (...,M,M): :return:\\|x\\| (...,1)"
msgstr ""

#: 1b00de398fdf4873839338da3f7176c1
msgid ""
"calculate the sign and log of the determinant of x. :param x (...,M,M): "
":return sign, x's logdet. sign array decides the sign of determinant and "
"their values can be -1,0,1.Only Real number now.0 means det is 0 and logdet "
"is -inf. logdet in shape (...,1)."
msgstr ""

#: 3081d936ef954da4ad3ae298369ac2b8
msgid ""
"do Cholesky decomposition of x in the form of below formula: x = LL^T x must"
" be a Hermite and positive-definite matrix. L is a lower-triangular matrix. "
":param x (...,M,M): :return: L (...,M,M)."
msgstr ""

#: 15e1de4bf1f14c989a7db49816a52305
msgid ""
"Solve a linear matrix equation Ax = B.This is done by calculating x = "
"A^-1B.So A must not be singular. :param a:(...,M,M) :param b:(...,M) "
":return:solution of Ax = b formula.x in the shape of (...M)"
msgstr ""

#: 1bcf6b9e1ac246d08e067079f45659b2
msgid ""
"do the qr factorization of x in the below formula: x = QR where Q is "
"orthogonal matrix and R is upper-triangle matrix. :param x (...,M,M): "
":return:q,r as the result of qr factorization.They are both in the shape of "
"(...,M,M)."
msgstr ""

#: e5c7891784604ea68434208329939e28
msgid ""
"Native jittor implementation: GEMM-shaped contractions dispatch to "
"``jt.matmul`` (cublas on GPU). Other cases are expressed with the existing "
"jittor tensor ops used by this implementation, including ``reindex`` for "
"diagonal handling, element-wise operations, reductions such as ``sum``, and "
"reshapes/transposes as needed. No numpy round-trip, so ``float16`` and "
"``bfloat16`` operands stay on-device throughout and autograd is provided by "
"the underlying jittor ops."
msgstr ""
